/-! GENERATED by gen_round_p.py (lane owner:b-weighted-level-9) from owner-8's frozen
`LevelJRound.lean`: the same round for an ARBITRARY level state `(yb, Mx)` at level `j`, with
the parameter identity `hP` where owner-8 used `runParameters j = PJ` by `rfl`. -/


/-! Lane owner:b-weighted-level-8, unit 2, segment 2d, piece 8: the level-`j` round with the
cost AND dims updates, on the same stack `H4` as `Level0DimsRound`, for the ACTUAL level `j` of
the run from the indexing seed (`yJ = (Iteration.run G c b (seedState b) j).budget`,
`MJ = (… j).matrix`, `PJ = stepParameters G c b yJ j MJ = runParameters G c b (seedState b) j`).

ONE fixed program `round4JProgram W w₀ v₀` = `LevelJPrep.prepJProgram` (lifted) ; the writer-22
program `W` (a parameter running on `H4`: it may read the previous round's output word, which
sits in the fresh cell `.inr 55`; its behaviour is the named premise `Writer22SpecJ`) ; owner-6
`costProgram` (by `costEmb4`) ; owner-7 `dimsProgram` (by `dimsEmb`) ; owner-5 `bridgeH`
(lifted); four charged handoffs.

Start bank: `ext4 (H0J (C1j G c b yJ j MJ mS)) (Dmw mw)` — the installed-words bank of level `j`
with master region `mS`, and the fresh region blank except cell 55 holding a word `mw` (the
previous round's output word; bound as the named input of `W`). Master hypotheses: `hV hN`
(|V| and blank row scratch) and `hmC hmB hmY hmE` (unary `c`, `b`, `yJ + j` = the level-`j`
cost word, `|E|`).

`level_dims_round_j`: ONE run halts on `ext4 (bank pEmb S2J z.stk) (DJ G c b yb j Mx mw)`: masters C,
B, Y, E hold the level-`(j+1)` raw words 0, 1, 2, 5; fresh cells 0, 1 hold words 3, 4; cell 55
still holds `mw`; plus the bridge-residue growth bound. -/

